<title>POLAND: WORK INJURIES UP 4.4 PCT IN POLAND IN 1996.</title>
<headline>WORK INJURIES UP 4.4 PCT IN POLAND IN 1996.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poles had 4.4 percent more workplace injuries last year than in 1995, with 10.3 out of every 1000 workers suffering injuries, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said on Monday.</p>
<p>GUS said in a report that out of the total 117,100 people injured at work last year, nearly 50,000 were hurt in production and 13,000 in construction.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
